@ The import table every overlay takes its stubs from: one far-call stub for
@ each routine of the main image a scene calls, under the name the scene
@ calls it by. An overlay's own table is this list cut down by the build to
@ the names its code calls and does not define, in this order: Camelot's
@ four divide routines, then the far-call entries in the order of the main
@ image (games/tbs/src/gamepak/far_call, by bank). NAME is the name of
@ the routine TARGET reaches, so overlays call the main image's routines by
@ their own names. The exceptions are the divide routines, which overlays
@ call under the compiler's names and the Math_ names, and the few routines
@ whose calls in the maps differ from their prototypes
@ (games/tbs/include/field/event.h says how).
	.syntax unified
	.thumb
	.balign 4
	.include "games/tbs/src/gamepak/far_call/veneer.inc"
